## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

The sqlite heartbeats internal pair scan (find_lease, relay.ml:2999-3047) is last-row-wins with no ORDER BY and the released check examines only the final row - the B295 freshest-first/released-skip fix covered alias_of_session only. On a legacy pre-B295 DB holding a released shadow row with a higher rowid than the live row, a heartbeat whose handler pre-check passed still fails inside the backend: it releases the shadow and returns unknown_alias as HTTP 200/ok:false - without the lease_not_found re-register guidance B293 added. Self-healing after one failure per shadow row; permanent if gc is disabled (interval 0).

## Fix direction

Give the heartbeat SELECT the same ORDER BY last_seen DESC + released-skip treatment.

## Evidence

Server-core review 2026-09-17.